we sema down that semaphore to check loading is finished.

>> B8: Consider parent process P with child process C.  How do you
>> ensure proper synchronization and avoid race conditions when P
>> calls wait(C) before C exits?  After C exits?  How do you ensure
>> that all resources are freed in each case?  How about when P
>> terminates without waiting, before C exits?  After C exits?  Are
>> there any special cases?

We use semaphore to deal with this case. When P waits for C, we decrease
the semaphore when we call wait function, and the semaphore is increased
only when the child process exits. So, P would wait until C exits. If P
calls wait after C exits, P has no child for waiting so it would not wait.
Unless P terminates without waiting, all the resources are freed when the
process exits. When P terminates first without waiting, I set P to terminate
all the children. So the resources used by the childeren would be free.

